-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Running ATHENA from this tree
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This directory is the ATHENA runtime tree.  It contains Scheme programs,
packages, styles, tools, assets, and the executable under `bin/`.

ATHENA is currently maintained on Linux with Qt 6.  The default local launcher
uses native Wayland:

    cd ATHENA
    ./StartATHENA.sh

`StartATHENA.sh`, `StartATHENA.qt6.sh`, and `StartATHENA.qt6.wayland.sh` are
currently equivalent.  They run:

    ./bin/ATHENA.bin --platform wayland

Any arguments passed to the launcher are forwarded to `ATHENA.bin`:

    ./StartATHENA.sh --no-splash-screen
    ./StartATHENA.sh /path/to/document.ath

The Wayland launcher deliberately does not force fcitx or Qt scale override
environment variables.  Qt should use its native Wayland input context, and
KDE/KWin should provide the output scale.  The launcher clears the common Qt
scale override knobs that previously caused wrong HiDPI behavior:

    unset QT_IM_MODULE
    unset GTK_IM_MODULE
    unset XMODIFIERS
    export QT_AUTO_SCREEN_SCALE_FACTOR=0
    unset QT_SCALE_FACTOR
    unset QT_SCREEN_SCALE_FACTORS
    unset QT_FONT_DPI
    unset QT_SCALE_FACTOR_ROUNDING_POLICY

It also prepends the local runtime library directory:

    export LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$script_dir/lib${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH}"

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Local development builds
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

From the repository root, configure a Qt 6 build.  A typical debug build uses
`build_qt6/`:

    cmake -S . -B build_qt6 -G Ninja \
      -DATHENA_GUI=Qt6 \
      -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug

No system Guile installation is needed. CMake builds ATHENA's vendored private
Guile 3 runtime and links the executable to it.

ATHENA patches Qt Advanced Docking System through `patch_ads.py`.  Reapply the
ADS patch after configuring or refreshing the dependency tree:

    python3 patch_ads.py build_qt6/_deps/ads-src

Build and install the local development binary into this runtime tree:

    cmake --build build_qt6 -j"$(nproc)"
    cp -f build_qt6/src/ATHENA.bin ATHENA/bin/ATHENA.bin
    cp -f build_qt6/src/athena-codex-bridge ATHENA/bin/athena-codex-bridge
    mkdir -p ATHENA/lib
    cp -a build_qt6/x64/lib/libqt6advanceddocking*.so* ATHENA/lib/

For debug ADS builds the library name may contain a `d` suffix, such as
`libqt6advanceddockingd.so`.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Release builds
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

For a release build, use a separate build directory such as `build_rel/` and
configure it explicitly for Qt 6.  The current local release workflow uses Intel
oneAPI when available:

    cmake -S . -B build_rel -G Ninja \
      -DATHENA_GUI=Qt6 \
      -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
      -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=/opt/intel/oneapi/compiler/latest/bin/icx \
      -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=/opt/intel/oneapi/compiler/latest/bin/icpx

Pass any local dependency paths required by your machine, such as llama.cpp,
resvg, or KIO options.  Reapply the ADS patch and build:

    python3 patch_ads.py build_rel/_deps/ads-src
    cmake --build build_rel -j"$(nproc)"

Use the idempotent all-platform release driver:

    tools/release/build-all.sh

For a native Linux runtime and tarball only:

    tools/release/build-all.sh --skip-container --skip-windows

This produces `release/ATHENA/`.  It is a runtime directory, not necessarily a
fully portable bundle: libraries already present in `ATHENA/lib` are copied, and
other libraries may still be resolved from the target system unless you package
them separately.

The release driver deliberately excludes formula cleaner, embedding, artifact
classification, and other model weights from all primary packages. It also
excludes virtual environments and generated Python caches. Do not replace this
step with a raw copy of `ATHENA/`; use:

    tools/release/runtime_policy.py verify release/ATHENA

to audit an assembled runtime.

OpenAI Codex integration always builds the lightweight
`athena-codex-bridge`.  It normally discovers a system `codex` executable.  A
redistributable Codex binary may instead be bundled explicitly:

    -DATHENA_BUNDLE_CODEX=ON \
    -DATHENA_CODEX_BINARY=/path/to/codex \
    -DATHENA_CODEX_LICENSE_FILE=/path/to/Codex/LICENSE

CMake refuses bundled-Codex builds without both the executable and its license.
The executable is installed beside ATHENA's binaries and the license is placed
under `licenses/codex/`.  Packagers remain responsible for verifying that the
selected Codex artifact and accompanying notices permit redistribution.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Container and AppImage builds
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

For redistributable Linux builds, use the scripted container build:

    tools/container-build/build-athena-container.sh

The script builds inside an openSUSE Leap 16.0 Podman environment, uses Qt 6,
builds the vendored private ATHENA Guile runtime, prefers Intel icx/icpx when
available, and produces:

    container_build/ATHENA-dev/
    container_build/ATHENA-rel/
    container_build/ATHENA-dev.AppImage
    container_build/ATHENA-rel.AppImage
    container_build/ATHENA-dev.AppImage.sha256
    container_build/ATHENA-rel.AppImage.sha256
    container_build/packages/*.deb
    container_build/packages/*-linux-x86_64.rpm

By default it also validates both AppImages in an Ubuntu 24.04 container:

    tools/container-build/validate-appimages-ubuntu.sh

The native package validator checks archive contents only and never installs an
RPM or DEB on the build host:

    tools/container-build/validate-native-packages.sh

The AppImage launch path defaults to Wayland in the same spirit as
`StartATHENA.qt6.wayland.sh`. The AppImage already contains ATHENA's complete
relocatable Scheme bytecode. DEB and RPM installation compiles the same Scheme
corpus once during the package post-install phase and stores it below
`/var/cache/athena`; normal startup does not compile it again.

`tools/release/build-all.sh` invokes this workflow for both `dev` and `rel`,
copies its AppImages and native packages into `release/` using canonical names,
and regenerates their SHA-256 files.

Useful environment variables for the container build include:

    ATHENA_BUILD_JOBS=16
    ATHENA_SKIP_UBUNTU_VALIDATE=1
    ATHENA_ALLOW_SYSTEM_COMPILER=1

The private Guile library, standard library, and compiled standard library are
bundled under `ATHENA/lib/athena-guile`; no target-system Guile is required.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Platform status
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Linux with Qt 6 and native Wayland is the primary maintained configuration.
KDE/Wayland is the most tested desktop path.

WSL2/WSLg can run the Linux AppImage or runtime tree when the required Linux
libraries and graphics stack are available.  Treat WSLg as a Linux/Wayland
environment, not as a native Win32 port.

Native Windows support is experimental and uses the separate tooling under
`tools/windows-deps/`.

Legacy non-Qt GUI backends have been removed from the maintained path.  The old
XCB launcher settings are no longer the default runtime configuration.
